## 5. Database Schema (Prisma)

### Enums
| Enum | Values |
|------|--------|
| `Role` | `MANAGER`, `ADMIN` |
| `AttendanceStatus` | `PRESENT`, `ABSENT`, `STANDBY` |
| `RouteAllocationStatus` | `ASSIGNED`, `UNASSIGNED`, `COMPLETED` |
| `LedgerTransactionType` | `SALARY`, `ADVANCE`, `PETROL_ALLOWANCE`, `SHORTAGE`, `EXTRA_PAID`, `MISC` |

### Models

#### `Manager`
The app user. Has `email` (unique), `passwordHash`, `role`, `branchName`.
Relation: has many `AttendanceRecord` (records they marked).

#### `DeliveryPerson`
Milk delivery staff. Key fields: `dpCode` (unique, auto-gen like `DP1001`), `isActive` (soft delete flag), all KYC fields (Aadhar, license, vehicle, bank, etc.).
Relations: attendance records, route allocations, assigned routes, empty bottle logs, ledger transactions.

#### `Route`
A delivery route. Fields: `name`, `zone`, `defaultPetrolAllowance`, `customerCount`, `litres`, `assignedDpId?` (the "permanent" default DP).
Relations: daily allocations, empty bottle logs, ledger transactions.

#### `AttendanceRecord`
Daily attendance per DP. Unique on `(dpId, date)`. Status is `PRESENT|ABSENT|STANDBY`.

#### `RouteAllocation`
Daily route assignment. Unique on `(routeId, date)`. Contains: `dpId`, `litresAllocated`, `qty1LBottle`, `qtyHalfLBottle`, `qtyHalfLPacket`, `petrolAllowanceGiven?`, `status`.

#### `InventoryItem`
Master list of inventory items (e.g., "1L Bottle", "500ml Packet"). Has `name`, `unit`, `material`.

#### `InventoryDailyRecord`
Daily snapshot per inventory item. Unique on `(inventoryItemId, date)`. Fields: `expectedStock`, `currentStock`, `carriedOverStock`, `newStockAdded`.

#### `EmptyBottleLog`
Evening return log per route per day. Unique on `(routeId, date)`. Fields: `deliveryCompleted`, `oneLBottlesCollected`, `halfLBottlesCollected`, `flagIssue`.

#### `DispatchDay`
The daily dispatch progress record. Unique on `date`. Has three nullable timestamps: `attendanceCompletedAt`, `inventoryCompletedAt`, `routesCompletedAt`. When all three are set → dispatch is complete.

#### `LedgerTransaction`
Financial entries. Links to a DP (optional) and a Route (optional). Type covers all financial event types.

