## 6. Full Daily Workflow — Step by Step

This is what actually happens each morning from app open to DPs going on their routes.

```
MORNING (7:00 AM)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
1. Manager opens the app
   → SplashScreen calls checkInitialAuth()
   → Finds JWT in secure storage → navigates to /dashboard

2. Dashboard loads
   → attendanceProvider fetches GET /attendance?date=today
   → routeProvider fetches GET /routes?date=today
   → dispatchProvider fetches GET /dispatch/summary?date=today
   → dashboardProvider (derived) computes counts from attendance + routes
   → Manager sees: 12 DPs total, 0 present, 12 routes unassigned

3. Manager taps "Morning Dispatch" button → /dispatch

4. DispatchReadyScreen shows 3 steps:
   [✗] Attendance   [✗] Inventory   [✗] Routes

STEP A: Attendance
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
5. Manager taps "Mark Attendance" → /dispatch/attendance

6. AttendanceScreen shows list of all DPs
   Manager taps each DP: PRESENT / ABSENT / STANDBY

7. Each tap calls attendanceProvider.markAttendance(dpId, status):
   → Optimistic UI update (instant)
   → PUT /attendance/:dpId { status: 'PRESENT' }
   → Backend upserts AttendanceRecord
   → Backend calls checkAndUpdateAttendanceCompletion()
   → If all DPs marked → DispatchDay.attendanceCompletedAt = now()

8. Manager goes back to DispatchReadyScreen
   → dispatchProvider invalidated → re-fetches
   → Step A now shows [✓] Attendance (with timestamp)

STEP B: Inventory Count
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
9. Manager taps "Check Inventory" → /dispatch/inventory

10. InventoryScreen loads via inventoryProvider:
    → GET /inventory?date=today
    → Backend auto-creates records with carry-forward if not yet present
    → e.g., "Yesterday's 1L bottle stock: 240 remaining → today's expected: 240"

11. Manager physically counts bottles in the store room
    → Updates each item's "Counted" number using +/– buttons
    → Or types directly in the field

12. Manager taps "Save Inventory"
    → inventoryProvider.saveInventory()
    → PUT /inventory { records: [{inventoryItemId, currentStock}, ...] }
    → Backend bulk upserts InventoryDailyRecord
    → Backend calls checkAndUpdateInventoryCompletion()
    → DispatchDay.inventoryCompletedAt = now()

13. Variance shows in red/green:
    → expectedQty=240 but counted 235 → variance=-5 (shortage)

STEP C: Route Allocation
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
14. Manager taps "Assign Routes" → /dispatch/routes

15. RouteAllocationScreen shows all routes with assigned DP or "Unassigned" badge

16. Manager taps a route → opens assignment bottom sheet
    → Selects which DP will run this route
    → Sets litres allocated
    → Opens MilkAllocationSheet (optional) → sets 1L, halfL, halfL-packet qty
    → Sets petrol allowance amount

17. Manager taps "Confirm Assignment"
    → routeProvider.assignRoute(routeId, dpId, ...)
    → PUT /routes/:routeId/allocation { dpId, litresAllocated, qty1LBottle, ..., petrolAllowanceGiven }
    → Backend:
       ① Checks inventory has enough bottles
       ② Upserts RouteAllocation record
       ③ Decrements inventory currentStock by qty
       ④ Creates LedgerTransaction (PETROL_ALLOWANCE / SHORTAGE / EXTRA_PAID)
       ⑤ Calls checkAndUpdateRoutesCompletion()

18. routeProvider invalidates inventoryProvider (stock changed)
    → InventoryScreen would now show updated currentStock

19. When all routes are assigned:
    → DispatchDay.routesCompletedAt = now()
    → DispatchReadyScreen shows all 3 steps complete

20. DPs physically leave for their routes (real world)

EVENING (6:00 PM - 8:00 PM)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
21. DPs return with empty bottles
    Manager taps "Evening Check" on dashboard → /evening-check

22. EveningCheckScreen loads via eveningCheckProvider:
    → GET /empty-bottles?date=today
    → Shows: Route A: expected 120 bottles, returned 0

23. For each returning DP, manager taps the route card → bottom sheet
    → Ticks "Delivery Completed"
    → Enters 1L bottles returned: 118
    → Enters 500ml bottles returned: 45
    → Optionally flags an issue

24. eveningCheckProvider.updateStatus(routeId, ...)
    → PUT /empty-bottles/:routeId { deliveryCompleted: true, oneLBottlesCollected: 118, ... }
    → Backend upserts EmptyBottleLog
    → Backend sets RouteAllocation.status = COMPLETED

25. routeProvider is invalidated → refreshes routes
    → Route A now shows as "Completed"

END OF DAY — Reports
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
26. Manager taps "Reports" → /reports → /dp-performance

27. DpPerformanceScreen loads via dpPerformanceProvider:
    → GET /reports/dp-performance?range=month&sortBy=litres
    → Shows ranking of all DPs by litres delivered this month

28. Manager views Ledger → /transactions
    → ledgerProvider loads → GET /ledger
    → Shows all petrol allowance transactions with shortage/extra flags
```

